<title>INDONESIA: Bimantara denies talk on food unit sale.</title>
<headline>Bimantara denies talk on food unit sale.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian conglomerate PT Bimantara Citra on Friday denied market rumours that it planned to sell its stake in food unit PT Nestle Indonesia to snack food firm PT Mayora Indah.</p>
<p>&quot;Bimantara Citra has no intention to sell off its shares in Nestle Indonesia to any company or to Mayora Indah as rumoured,&quot; Bimantara said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;Nestle Indonesia is a high growth and strong cash flow company. To date, Bimantara Citra owns a 20 percent stake in Nestle Indonesia,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>Bimantara rose 25 rupiah to 4,350 rupiah, while Mayora gained 25 rupiah to 1,100 rupiah at 0845 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
